@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+# DRAFT SCAFFOLD — 2D superconductor characterization by transport (BBG/WSe2)
+
+*Investigation recipe, v0 scaffold. Grows as we walk papers. Structure follows the house
+investigation skeleton (`recipes/investigations/trilayer-stacking-id.md`): What / When / Why
+/ Recipe / Verify / Examples / Next, with confounds inline and a mandatory output contract.
+Not yet STYLE-conformed; not rig/device-specific yet. `[TODO]` marks slots for incoming
+papers / decisions. Promote to `recipes/investigations/` once fleshed out and STYLE-conformed.*
+
+**System:** dual-graphite-gated Bernal bilayer graphene proximitized by WSe2. Goal:
+identify and characterize gate-tuned proximity-induced superconductivity. Toploader (base T
+≪ Tc; Tc ~ O(100 mK) expected for non-moiré graphene SCs).
+
+## References (ingested papers)
+- `../papers/2106.07640/paper.md` — RTG SC (Zhou 2021): the prototypical 2D-transport SC
+  characterization flow + its epistemics. **Read first.**
+- `[TODO]` BBG/WSe2 superconductivity paper(s) — phenomenology, where the domes sit.
+- `[TODO]` WSe2→graphene proximity SOC + twist-angle dependence — for the forward model.
+- `[TODO]` Bernal-bilayer isospin/Stoner phase diagram — the normal state the SC lives on.
+
+## What
+Establish whether a gate-tuned low-Rxx region is a **superconductor**, distinguish it from a
+**failed superconductor / anomalous metal**, and characterize it (critical values, field
+response, normal-state fermiology). Output: per-candidate, evidence-cited, **hedged** call on
+the STYLE strength scale + extracted properties — never a bare "SC here."
+
+## When
+- A BBG/WSe2 device is loaded, gated, (n, D) calibrated, with ≥1 credible four-terminal Rxx
+  channel. `[TODO: device-init prerequisites — gate calibration, CNP, validators.]`
+- Candidate low-Rxx regions appear in the (n, D) map, or proximity-SC is the campaign goal.
+
+## Why
+- **SC is a constellation call** (see paper notes): no single hallmark suffices; corroborate
+  zero/low Rxx + nonlinear IV + field response + T-dependence + phase coherence + fermiology.
+- **The fork that sets the bar:** low-but-finite Rxx may be a genuine *failed SC / anomalous
+  metal* (Kapitulnik–Kivelson–Spivak), not just an unconfirmed SC.
+- **The SC sits on a specific normal state** — fermiology (fan/FFT) is part of the
+  characterization, not an afterthought. `[TODO: BBG-specific normal-state expectations.]`
+
+## Recipe
+*Ordering principle: do everything achievable AT BASE T first; heat up for T-dependence
+LAST (the thermal cycle is the expensive step).*
+
+**Step 0 — mine what's already on disk.** Existing maps/fans/IV curves before proposing any
+sweep.
+
+**Step 1 — pristine-flux gate map, BEFORE energizing the magnet.**
+- Rxx(n, D) low-Rxx spots = candidates.
+- **Trapped-flux protocol (load-bearing):** superconducting magnets retain O(1 mT) trapped
+  flux — enough to kill these fragile SCs; the magnet's nominal zero is NOT true zero field.
+  Sample loading (probe system) warms the magnet above its own Tc; on re-cooling it traps
+  ~0 (cooled in Earth's field). **Take the first map before touching the magnet** — once you
+  sweep the field controller you inject trapped flux — so a weak SC isn't erased by a stray
+  mT. *(Magnet trapped-flux magnitude / loading-reset = rig fact → rig card; map-first
+  ordering = protocol → here.)*
+- Coarse→fine: gate maps are slow; reconnoiter coarse, zoom into candidates.
+
+**Step 2 — nonlinear characterization (base T).** dV/dI vs I_dc on each candidate.
+- **Confound:** the dV/dI critical-current-like peak is NOT SC-specific — non-equilibrium
+  criticality (Zener–Schwinger, Berdyugin–Geim 2022) and QH breakdown mimic it.
+  Consistent-with, not evidence-for.
+
+**Step 3 — field characterization (base T).**
+- **Find true B = 0 from the SC itself** (it's strongest at genuine zero field → maximize SC
+  / minimize Rxx) once any flux is trapped.
+- B_c⊥ (→ ξ via Hc2 = Φ₀/2πξ², *order-of-magnitude only*); B_c∥.
+- **Field-killing is also a candidate confirmation:** a small B⊥ that removes the low Rxx
+  while leaving the normal state ≈unchanged supports the SC reading.
+- Phase-coherent (Fraunhofer-like) oscillations vs B⊥: report as "consistent with phase
+  coherence," extract the implied area (Φ₀/area), do NOT name it Fraunhofer or over-read the
+  microscopic origin (weak-link vs finite-size geometry both viable).
+- *Pauli caveat:* if B_c∥ exceeds 1.86 Tc, do not call it a Pauli violation / triplet
+  signature on that basis alone (weak-coupling-BCS yardstick).
+
+**Step 4 — normal-state fermiology (base T).** Landau fan Rxx(n, B⊥) → FFT of Rxx(1/B).
+- SdH discipline: work in 1/B; low-field data is high-leverage (record length sets Δf);
+  **FFT hygiene = stability sweep** (vary detrender + windowing — real peak sharpens
+  vertically as record lengthens, artifact wanders; scale matters, detrender choice doesn't);
+  window bounded both ends (onset/mobility below, QH distortion + finite-field transitions
+  above).
+- Mobility sanity: μ ≳ 1/B_onset (≈10⁴/B_onset[T] cm²/Vs); transport → lower bound.
+- Identify which normal-state phase the SC sits on. `[TODO: BBG normal-state phases &
+  expected SdH signatures; forward model — parked, WSe2 twist-angle dependence is the hard
+  part.]`
+
+**Step 5 — temperature characterization (HEAT UP — last).**
+- Tc/T_BKT via the extraction ladder (V∝I³ exponent crossing rigorous; %-threshold
+  convention; Halperin–Nelson often poor → hedge).
+- ξ from Hc2(T) is the proper route but rounds (→ underestimated T-dependence); quantum
+  geometry also affects ξ → keep ξ order-of-magnitude.
+
+**Step 6 — the call.** Output contract `[TODO: finalize, mirror trilayer recipe]`:
+1. Per-candidate verdict on the STYLE strength scale (SC / failed-SC–anomalous-metal /
+   not-SC), each with a weight word.
+2. Evidence list: each hallmark with (n, D, B, T) coordinates and the paper panel/benchmark.
+3. Confidence + specific hedges (which hallmarks present, which searched-and-absent vs
+   not-resolvable).
+4. What would firm the call.
+5. A reasoned "cannot tell" is success; a confident call without hallmark-level evidence is
+   a protocol violation.
+
+## Verify
+- Constellation corroboration (no single-hallmark calls).
+- True-zero-field via the SC (trapped-flux aware).
+- FFT stability sweep for any fermiology claim.
+- Pauli / Fraunhofer / ξ over-read guards (above).
+- `[TODO: TSV-first re-forming of channels; aliasing robustness; forward-model overlay once
+  the BBG+SOC model exists.]`
+
+## Examples
+- `[TODO]` our BBG/WSe2 campaign, once it runs (mechanical facts only, per STYLE).
+
+## Next
+- **SC-confirmed:** full characterization campaign (field, fermiology, T) → the physics.
+- **Failed-SC / anomalous-metal-leaning:** the interesting fork — design the measurements
+  that separate it from true SC.
+- **Resolution-limited cannot-tell:** state base-T / field / mobility limits; a rig/device
+  question, not more sweeps.
