+# VTI kernel compatibility — vendored vti_drivers vs measurement-env
+
+**Date**: 2026-06-09, for the 2026-06-10 QC0426 live session.
+**Verdict: NO HARD INCOMPATIBILITY.** The full operator API
+(`set_basedir` / `async_station` / `fp` / `sweep` / `megasweep` /
+`multisweep` / `multimegasweep` / `add_comment`) works against the
+sharpelab measureme fork with **signatures identical to the rig's installed
+sweep** (verified by `inspect.signature` on both sides). Plan B (registering
+the rig's system Python as a kernelspec) should not be needed.
+
+Two things to act on before tomorrow (details in "Shims / actions" at
+bottom): **(1)** kernel Python must be **>= 3.12** (FastBi1K5.py uses
+PEP 701 f-strings — SyntaxError on 3.10/3.11; env's requires-python floor
+is 3.10 and there is no `.python-version` pin); **(2)** metadata written by
+our kernel is **schema v2** — multisweep/multimegasweep key names go plural
+(`params`, `slow_params`, `fast_params`) and `version`/`instruments` keys
+are added. `sweep.sweep_load.pload` reads both v1 (rig) and v2 (ours)
+transparently, but any of Qingrui's analysis cells that index
+`metadata['slow_param']` directly will KeyError on **new** runs.
+
