+| 4b | Operator API signatures | **PASS** | `sweep(param, setpoints, delay=0.0)`, `megasweep(slow_param, slow_v, fast_param, fast_v, slow_delay=0.0, fast_delay=0.0, init_delay=True)`, `multisweep(params, setpointslist, delay=0.0)`, `multimegasweep(slow_params, slow_v_list, fast_params, fast_v_list, slow_delay=0.0, fast_delay=0.0, init_delay=True)`, `add_comment(str|dict)`, chained `s.fp(p)` — **byte-identical signatures to the rig's installed sweep** (checked live over ssh; rig sweep at `C:\Users\DGG\Documents\GitHub\measureme`). Sweeping `magnet.mag` (bound method with `.full_name='mag'`, not a qcodes Parameter) works: sweep code only calls `param(value)` and reads `.full_name`. |
+| 4b' | On-disk output format | **PASS w/ note** | Same layout: `data/<id>/data.tsv.gz` + `metadata.json`; same column order (`time`, slow…, fast…, followed params); verified by running real dummy sweeps and diffing against rig runs 79/80. Metadata is v2: adds `version` + `instruments` (instrument snapshots); multisweep writes `params` (rig: `param`), multimegasweep writes `slow_params`/`fast_params` (rig: `slow_param`/`fast_param`). All other keys (`comments`, `type`, `function`, delays, `columns`, `measurement_config`, setpoints, `interrupted`, `start_time`, `end_time`) identical. `pload`/`load_meta` migrate v1→v2 on read — confirmed loading rig run 80 (161×201 multimegasweep) and our v2 output. |
